  "id": "eye-structure",
  "term": "eye structure",
  "definition": "In this context, eye structure means the physical layout of the compound eye, including features such as overall eye size, facet size, and the angles between visual units. These structural differences affect visual sensitivity and spatial resolution, shaping how butterflies take in information from their environment for navigation and movement.",
